  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "Winter is three cold days in January that the parish talks about until March.",
      "By May the air is a warm wet towel, and it stays that way, without apology, past All Souls.",
      "August afternoons end in a thunderstorm you can set the evening Mass by, and then the steam comes up off the lot.",
      "September is hurricane season, and the whole diocese watches the Gulf with the attention it does not give to Lent."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "Sunday is six Masses in three languages in a building that was built for two Masses in one.",
      "The Spanish Mass overflows onto the sidewalk, and the Vietnamese choir rehearses in the hall while the Anglos take Communion.",
      "Everyone drives, from everywhere, and a family from the far side of Harris County calls itself a parishioner without irony."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of Houston are young, from five continents, and too tired to have formed an opinion of each other.",
      "A man's standing is measured in languages and in mortgages paid down, and nobody asks where he went to seminary.",
      "They meet at noodle shops and taquerias after the last Mass, and the talk is of building committees and rain."
    ]
  },
